# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
{ns}
{define: Asus2 base-fret 1 frets x 0 2 2 0 0}
{define: Asus4 base-fret 1 frets x 0 2 2 3 0}
{define: Esus base-fret 1 frets 0 2 2 2 0 0} 
{define: F#m base-fret 1 frets x x 4 2 2 2} 
{t: MY HOMETOWN (In D)}
{t:  Bruce Springsteen  }
{artist: Bruce Springsteen  }
{composer: Bruce Springsteen  }


https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=z6LABdHtkUA  (Capo 0)

Also available in G which you may find easier to play.

TIP:  The (Asus2) and (Esus) can be ignored in favor of just (A) and (E) but they’re easy to play as (Asus) is just (A) without the bottom finger and (Esus) is just (E) with your pinky added to the 3rd string/2nd fret.  The majors are played one syllable after the suspended.  

TIP:  Also note there’s an (Asus4) in the bridge.  Just slide your bottom finger up one fret or add your pinky to the 2nd fret/3rd string.

TIP:  (D) can be played instead of the (F#m) if you want.


